<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌧️ LIVE PRECIPITATION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/precipitation_na/legend.png?v=na-precip-20261029-0245-r13" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Precipitation type + intensity (OBSERVED radar echo; 5-75 dBZ severity). <b>Rain</b> ramp: dark green (light) &rarr; green &rarr; yellow &rarr; orange &rarr; red &rarr; magenta &rarr; purple (extreme). <b>Snow/Sleet</b> ramp: pale blue (light) &rarr; blue &rarr; purple (heavy). Same intensity sits at the same position on both ramps. Type is observed/analysed, never inferred from color: MRMS PrecipFlag (snow class 3) inside CONUS and the regional AK/HI/CARIB domains, ECCC SfcPrecipType (snow classes) in Canada, and GFS CSNOW/CICEP for model snow/ice in verified radar gaps only. Echoes from sources that publish no type (OPERA EU, JMA) stay on the Rain ramp. No echo = transparent; GFS pixels are model estimates, never radar. GFS model estimates (not radar) use the same two ramps where no radar covers.</p><p><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT OBSERVATION (MRMS CONUS + regional AK/HI/CARIB + ECCC NA radar, 2-6 min mosaic)</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NSSL MRMS SeamlessHSR hybrid-scan reflectivity composite (CONUS, Alaska, Hawaii, Caribbean; dBZ, public domain) + ECCC North American Radar Composite 1km rain (RADAR_1KM_RRAI, mm/h) / snow (RADAR_1KM_RSNO, cm/h) / precipitation type (Radar_1km_SfcPrecipType) + EUMETNET OPERA EU DBZH composite (CC BY 4.0) in remaining radar gaps + JMA Japan nowcast (attribution) in Japan gaps + NOAA GFS model estimates, same colors (public domain) in verified radar gaps only<br/><a href="https://mrms.ncep.noaa.gov/data/">https://mrms.ncep.noaa.gov/data/</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p><p><b>Coverage</b> — one at a time, switched right here in this folder:<br>◉ <b>Global Coverage</b> (shown)<br>○ Continental Coverage<br>○ Great Lakes Basin Coverage<br>Pro switches exclusively. Web/app: check exactly one box.</p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE PRECIPITATION</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/precipitation_na/legend.png?v=na-precip-20261029-0245-r13" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Precipitation type + intensity (OBSERVED radar echo; 5-75 dBZ severity). <b>Rain</b> ramp: dark green (light) &rarr; green &rarr; yellow &rarr; orange &rarr; red &rarr; magenta &rarr; purple (extreme). <b>Snow/Sleet</b> ramp: pale blue (light) &rarr; blue &rarr; purple (heavy). Same intensity sits at the same position on both ramps. Type is observed/analysed, never inferred from color: MRMS PrecipFlag (snow class 3) inside CONUS and the regional AK/HI/CARIB domains, ECCC SfcPrecipType (snow classes) in Canada, and GFS CSNOW/CICEP for model snow/ice in verified radar gaps only. Echoes from sources that publish no type (OPERA EU, JMA) stay on the Rain ramp. No echo = transparent; GFS pixels are model estimates, never radar. GFS model estimates (not radar) use the same two ramps where no radar covers.</p><p><b>Sources:</b> NOAA/NSSL MRMS SeamlessHSR hybrid-scan reflectivity composite (CONUS, Alaska, Hawaii, Caribbean; dBZ, public domain) + ECCC North American Radar Composite 1km rain (RADAR_1KM_RRAI, mm/h) / snow (RADAR_1KM_RSNO, cm/h) / precipitation type (Radar_1km_SfcPrecipType) + EUMETNET OPERA EU DBZH composite (CC BY 4.0) in remaining radar gaps + JMA Japan nowcast (attribution) in Japan gaps + NOAA GFS model estimates, same colors (public domain) in verified radar gaps only<br><b>Precedence:</b> ECCC rain (rates -> dBZ via NWS Z=300R^1.4 onto the shared severity scale) wins everywhere its RADAR_COVERAGE_*.INV dynamic coverage is valid, including most of CONUS; ECCC snow classes (SfcPrecipType) render on the Snow/Sleet ramp; NOAA/NSSL MRMS SeamlessHSR (CONUS + regional AK/HI/CARIB: measured dBZ -> severity ramps, PrecipFlag class 3 -> Snow/Sleet ramp) fills ECCC gaps; OPERA EU DBZH fills remaining non-NA radar gaps on the Rain ramp (no type product); JMA nowcast intensity (mm/h classes) fills Japan gaps via Z-R equivalents on the Rain ramp (no type product); GFS model estimates (CSNOW/CICEP -> Snow/Sleet ramp, CRAIN/CFRZR -> Rain ramp) only in verified radar gaps; transparent elsewhere.<br><b>Coverage:</b> Global Coverage<br><b>Radar note:</b> radar echoes (MRMS CONUS + regional AK/HI/CARIB/ECCC/OPERA/JMA); GFS model estimates (not radar) in verified radar gaps, same colors<br></p><p><b>Coverage</b> — one at a time, switched right here in this folder:<br>◉ <b>Global Coverage</b> (shown)<br>○ Continental Coverage<br>○ Great Lakes Basin Coverage<br>Pro switches exclusively. Web/app: check exactly one box.</p>]]></description>
      <Style>
        <ListStyle>
          <listItemType>radioFolder</listItemType>
        </ListStyle>
      </Style>
      <GroundOverlay>
        <name>Global Coverage</name>
        <visibility>1</visibility>
        <drawOrder>10</drawOrder>
        <Icon>
          <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/precipitation_na/current.png?v=na-precip-20261029-0245-r13</href>
          <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
          <refreshInterval>300</refreshInterval>
        </Icon>
        <LatLonBox>
          <north>90.0</north>
          <south>-90.0</south>
          <east>180.0</east>
          <west>-180.0</west>
        </LatLonBox>
      </GroundOverlay>
      <GroundOverlay>
        <name>Continental Coverage</name>
        <visibility>0</visibility>
        <drawOrder>11</drawOrder>
        <Icon>
          <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/precipitation_na_continental/current.png?v=na-precip-20261029-0245-r13</href>
          <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
          <refreshInterval>300</refreshInterval>
        </Icon>
        <LatLonBox>
          <north>90.0</north>
          <south>-90.0</south>
          <east>180.0</east>
          <west>-180.0</west>
        </LatLonBox>
      </GroundOverlay>
      <GroundOverlay>
        <name>Great Lakes Basin Coverage</name>
        <visibility>0</visibility>
        <drawOrder>12</drawOrder>
        <Icon>
          <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/precipitation_na_basin/current.png?v=na-precip-20261029-0245-r13</href>
          <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
          <refreshInterval>300</refreshInterval>
        </Icon>
        <LatLonBox>
          <north>85.0</north>
          <south>5.0</south>
          <east>-15.0</east>
          <west>-180.0</west>
        </LatLonBox>
      </GroundOverlay>
    </Folder>
  </Document>
</kml>
